                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d5d5204f-b942-4d77-9fbd-43162f2cf84c",
                        "entry_id": "cdb2f3d1-f272-3b64-bb3b-dc470b0c4926",
                        "tags": [
                            "singular",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "filandreuse"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "cad7adc4-52a1-4dd7-ab9e-59fe30adfd26",
                        "entry_id": "cdb2f3d1-f272-3b64-bb3b-dc470b0c4926",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "filandreuses"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d752804f-0c1e-32e4-a586-21fca819023b",
                        "entry_id": "cdb2f3d1-f272-3b64-bb3b-dc470b0c4926",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui est rempli de filandres, de fils, de fibres."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff18c43a-d3b6-488d-a22c-c7d5e7d5ee24",
                                "sense_id": "d752804f-0c1e-32e4-a586-21fca819023b",
                                "text": "Les petits vins blancs d’Allemagne agacent les nerfs, les gros vins rouges du Midi écœurent bien vite, les fruits manquent, les légumes sont durs, la viande filandreuse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7cb03078-5aab-4022-bed0-5192f96d8f74",
                                "sense_id": "d752804f-0c1e-32e4-a586-21fca819023b",
                                "text": "S’il y a des parties très filandreuses, récupérez la chair à l’aide d’une cuillère."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3a896082-c72c-301b-aa01-c9ee5878630c",
                        "entry_id": "cdb2f3d1-f272-3b64-bb3b-dc470b0c4926",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qualifie un style, un discours, dont les phrases sont longues et embarrassées."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "57b56f70-8491-4eca-a9f0-0a1e603c36a9",
                                "sense_id": "3a896082-c72c-301b-aa01-c9ee5878630c",
                                "text": "Les novateurs modernes écrivent des théories pâteuses, filandreuses et nébuleuses ou des romans philanthropiques ; mais le voleur pratique ! il est clair comme un fait, il est logique comme un coup de poing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0e22777-e92b-47bc-b89b-e0f7744915eb",
                                "sense_id": "3a896082-c72c-301b-aa01-c9ee5878630c",
                                "text": "Tous ceux qui assistent aux séances des Chambres reconnaîtront les habitudes de la lutte parlementaire dans ces phrases filandreuses avec lesquelles on calme les irritations en gagnant du temps."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a382e84d-6d79-4530-8357-2ef07a504f1d",
                                "sense_id": "3a896082-c72c-301b-aa01-c9ee5878630c",
                                "text": "C'est Ménard qui rend compte de La Chute dans Critique. Ce sera peut-être moins intelligent que du Bataille, mais aura l'avantage d'être moins filandreux ! Les naïfs ne gênent pas l'élan d'une œuvre...\" — (Albert Camus et René Char, Correspondance 1946-1959, Gallimard, Folio, 2017, page 167)"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5f0945ce-8ac3-3a9a-a062-d3c663c4fea6",
                        "entry_id": "cdb2f3d1-f272-3b64-bb3b-dc470b0c4926",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qualifie celui qui les profère."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "32a14fcc-ebf6-4b49-b062-b041df963a9a",
                                "sense_id": "5f0945ce-8ac3-3a9a-a062-d3c663c4fea6",
                                "text": "Un écrivain filandreux. - Un orateur filandreux."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d871157-55a2-45f6-a287-af9ce8b53a6e",
                                "sense_id": "5f0945ce-8ac3-3a9a-a062-d3c663c4fea6",
                                "text": "— Il est verbeux, il est filandreux. C’est un ouvrier en raisonnements, c’est un bon logicien ; mais il ne comprend pas la grande logique, celle des événements et des affaires."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b7143d25-31a5-4f5f-a1f6-5505b7a442d7",
                        "source_entry_id": "cdb2f3d1-f272-3b64-bb3b-dc470b0c4926",
                        "source_sense_id": "d752804f-0c1e-32e4-a586-21fca819023b",
                        "source_sense_description": "Qui est rempli de filandres",
                        "target_lang_word": "stringy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "stringy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "80c283ad-8862-3e27-813c-5e62f74d9372",
                                        "entry_id": "8b008df3-9824-3244-ac68-8bf010d7f766",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Composed of, or resembling, string or strings."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e6729be-8738-3f3c-83c1-aaa2c1a050b5",
                                        "entry_id": "8b008df3-9824-3244-ac68-8bf010d7f766",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tough to the bite, as containing too much sinew or string tissue."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of food"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b5182d2-b986-4d19-8f38-9aa2399aa05d",
                                                "sense_id": "9e6729be-8738-3f3c-83c1-aaa2c1a050b5",
                                                "text": "The meat was quite stringy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "69c7505a-d080-30e6-8374-0833be0b4412",
                                        "entry_id": "8b008df3-9824-3244-ac68-8bf010d7f766",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Wiry, lean, scrawny."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a person"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f82afe39-fc10-4dd4-af1c-564cbfa9333c",
                                                "sense_id": "69c7505a-d080-30e6-8374-0833be0b4412",
                                                "text": "The colonel and his sponsor made a queer contrast: Greystone [the sponsor] long and stringy, with a face that seemed as if a cold wind was eternally playing on it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0560520c-0ed0-4569-8dc8-2fc34dfda9cd",
                                                "sense_id": "69c7505a-d080-30e6-8374-0833be0b4412",
                                                "text": "\"I know, I know,\" said the man who had been addressed as Peeble, a nervous, stringy, dried-up person as he now appeared in the light."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6c3c8c85-c88a-39ff-b7d7-7a78df517b85",
                                        "entry_id": "8b008df3-9824-3244-ac68-8bf010d7f766",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Resembling or involving text strings."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bed8d5b7-0994-407d-b06c-af73604ce8ca",
                                                "sense_id": "6c3c8c85-c88a-39ff-b7d7-7a78df517b85",
                                                "text": "The context refers to how you use an expression. You've actually already seen some contextual operations with numbers and strings. When you do numbery sorts of things, you get numeric results. When you do stringy sorts of things, you get string results."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "25987486-896d-3f8f-baf5-a7fa2d7497e3",
                                        "entry_id": "8b008df3-9824-3244-ac68-8bf010d7f766",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a sighting, unlikely to be accurate; probably based on a misidentification, whether innocent or deliberate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dda264c0-a102-4052-9539-5b855664272c",
                                                "sense_id": "25987486-896d-3f8f-baf5-a7fa2d7497e3",
                                                "text": "There are few birders who have not had stringy ticks on their lists at some stage."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "94cc0aa7-f49c-4b6e-b6cd-487fffa3ef33",
                        "source_entry_id": "cdb2f3d1-f272-3b64-bb3b-dc470b0c4926",
